When `dumptxoutset` creates a rollback snapshot, the copy loop skips coins on read failure. The cursor catches the new decompression exception and returns false, so this PR
      adds another trigger for that issue. Could we abort the copy on a failed read, either here or in a separate follow-up? Otherwise, `dumptxoutset` can succeed with a coin missing.


`scantxoutset` uses the same cursor reader, but a failed read currently looks like cancellation (`success: false` with partial results). Could we return the UTXO read error there as well?
      The existing corruption test can cover both RPCs before triggering the validation abort.

